red. Clear age discrimination and unresolved follow-up needed.\\n\\n**DEV-032:** Age-based rejection with explicit discrimination (\\\"want someone older because younger staff can't be trusted with money\\\"). Open request for reconsideration unanswered. Clear age discrimination and unresolved follow-up.\\n\\n**DEV-033:** Procedural failure (missed interview, no response to rebook request). Candidate mentions religion but makes no explicit connection to the missed call or discrimination. No explicit discrimination allegation. Open rebook request unanswered.\\n\\n**DEV-034:** Identical procedural failure as DEV-033 (missed interview, no response to rebook request). Religion mentioned but no explicit discrimination connection. Open rebook request unanswered.\\n\\n**DEV-035:** Specific, concrete sexual harassment: unwanted touching (thigh) that continued after the candidate moved away, plus quid pro quo statement about hiring. Explicit request to report.\\n\\n**DEV-036:** Explicit discrimination (racist remarks by panel) plus retaliatory withdrawal of application specifically because the candidate complained. Explicit request for review. This is both discriminatory treatment and adverse action linked to a discrimination complaint.\\n\\n**DEV-037:** Explicit disability-based exclusion: recruiter stated \\\"don't interview wheelchair users\\\" and cancelled the appointment. Accessibility arrangement requested but explicitly refused. Explicit request for review.\\n\\n**DEV-038:** Requested accessibility accommodation was provided appropriately (ground-floor room, route pre-checked). Candidate explicitly states this \\\"made the interview much easier.\\\" Concrete favorable example, well-resolved.\\n\\n**DEV-039:** Intrusive demand for psychiatric diagnoses and medication before assessment, with no stated occupational-health or accommodation context. Candidate requested explanation and received none. Specific intrusive medical inquiry without justification.\\n\\n**DEV-040:** Routine, appropriate accommodation-check question. Candidate declined. Factual account with no evaluation or unresolved issue.\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"context_management\":null,\"diagnostics\":null,\"id\":\"msg_011CfVeKrzN6RL4Pnin7WVyN\",\"input_transformations\":[],\"model\":\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"stop_details\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"type\":\"message\",\"usage\":{\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":4541,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4541,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\",\"input_tokens\":10,\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"}},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"request_id\":\"req_011CfVeKrcJEm2PPToJxANYw\",\"session_id\":\"d2a523e3-576e-4c4c-a44a-039988872bee\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-28T10:02:05.836Z\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"cd29b94e-63e4-462b-b57d-7a250824813d\"},{\"message\":{\"container\":null,\"content\":[{\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"},\"id\":\"toolu_01HkJPy8fSfnVBGKUerjQUyD\",\"input\":{\"records\":[{\"follow_up_needed\":\"yes\",\"id\":\"DEV-031\",\"sentiment\":\"negative\",\"serious_concern_reported\":\"yes\",\"testimonial_potential\":\"no\"},{\"follow_up_needed\":\"yes\",\"id\":\"DEV-032\",\"sentiment\":\"negative\",\"serious_concern_reported\":\"yes\",\"testimonial_potential\":\"no\"},{\"follow_up_needed\":\"yes\",\"id\":\"DEV-033\",\"sentiment\":\"negative\",\"serious_concern_reported\":\"no\",\"testimonial_potential\":\"no\"},{\"follow_up_needed\":\"yes\",\"id\":\"DEV-034\",\"sentiment\":\"negative\",\"serious_concern_reported\":\"no\",\"testimonial_potential\":\"no\"},{\"follow_up_needed\":\"yes\",\"id\":\"DEV-035\",\"sentiment\":\"negative\",\"serious_concern_reported\":\"yes\",\"testimonial_potential\":\"no\"},{\"follow_up_needed\":\"yes\",\"id\":\"DEV-036\",\"sentiment\":\"negative\",\"serious_concern_reported\":\"yes\",\"testimonial_potential\":\"no\"},{\"follow_up_needed\":\"yes\",\